---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { meta } from "../../data/pages";
---
<Layout {...meta("/blog/")}>
  <article class="frame prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Field notes</p>
    <h1 class="display">Notes from building Torana.</h1>
    <p>Experiments, architectural detours, and the occasional “how did this become a plugin runtime?”</p>
    <ul class="article-list">
    <li>
      <h2><a href="/blog/local-models-tool-output/">Scan tool output for PII with a local model.</a></h2>
      <p>Set up the PII plugin to check for exposed keys, passwords and private data. Compare the local scanners tested, including their misses and false positives.</p>
      <p class="article-meta">4 October 2026 · local models · PII · hands-on guide</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h2><a href="/blog/why-torana/">This was supposed to be a compactor.</a></h2>
      <p>How an experiment in compacting tool outputs became a local-first, programmable proxy—with a little architectural scope creep along the way.</p>
      <p class="article-meta">Building Torana · the origin story</p>
    </li>
    <li>
    <h2><a href="/blog/context-compaction-negative-result/">I removed 4.8 MB from my coding agent's requests. The bill barely moved.</a></h2>
    <p>The compactor that broke file edits, the one I measured over 75 sessions, and why cheap prompt caching made repeated tool output nearly free. Plus what's next: other providers and per-tool-call decisions.</p>
    <p class="muted">26 July 2026, updated 8 October 2026 · context · prompt caching · negative result</p>
    </li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Layout>
